WEBVTT

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:03.600
So you were a spy?

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:05.910
When did you turn?

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:08.110
Were those tears fake?

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:10.040
Tears?

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:14.390
When you saw the islanders being 
burned by the Mongols two days ago,

00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:16.310
you cried.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:21.330
You're more of a softie 
than I thought you'd be.

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:23.690
I wasn't lying.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:27.320
I told you. The same thing happened to me.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.330
A neighboring lord tricked me and

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.990
made everyone think I was a villain.

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:34.510
I lost everything.

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:36.770
I was driven from my lands,

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:39.010
and all the people I knew were
separated from one another.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:45.780
I realized too late that it's always those 
close to you who desire your downfall.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:50.290
I wasn't really doing everything I could.

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:55.430
I'm fighting to get back 
my clan and my lands.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:57.760
I don't care what I have 
to do to make it happen.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:01.340
Here I come, Kuchii Jinzaburou!

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:04.540
Let's fight, then.

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:40.430
<i>Your katana...</i>

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:42.480
<i>And my naginata.</i>

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:45.840
<i>Of course, I have the advantage 
with my longer range.</i>

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:48.170
<i>I'll use it...</i>

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:50.170
<i>...to win!</i>

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:54.110
<i>You dodged it?</i>

00:02:54.470 --> 00:02:58.820
<i>Then you'll try and get right up next to me.</i>

00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:03.030
<i>If I drop my weapon and dodge this attack,</i>

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:05.040
<i>I can kill you!</i>

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:22.420
That was clever.

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:24.140
Gikei style.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:26.660
I should've known I stood no chance.

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:31.050
Revenge for those of us who died.

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:32.390
For Onami.

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:36.270
You'll pay for betraying us! 
For betraying this island!

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:38.110
Stay out of this! 
You're not worthy of interfering!

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:41.560
Tatsu, leave them.

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:44.290
Let the exiles handle their own affairs.

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:52.290
I can see countless souls 
of the dead clinging to your arm...

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:55.350
I'll be one of them, too.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.560
Now, take my head!

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:04.850
I'm glad I was able to learn 
that your tears weren't false ones.

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:10.450
The person who fought 
by my side then was the real you.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.980
I'm glad I was able to learn that.

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:15.070
Just five days ago,

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:18.240
we were empty shells,

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:20.770
tossed about on a tiny boat in the sea.

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:24.310
But once we came to this island,

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:26.820
we were able to fight again.

00:04:27.170 --> 00:04:30.910
You in your way, and I in mine.

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:33.720
You're right.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:37.020
And it's thanks to you.

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:41.030
Save this island.

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:43.910
I will.

00:05:06.050 --> 00:05:08.230
Where should this head go?

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:10.830
I'll take it.

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:13.250
Princess!

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:22.040
Exile Shiraishi Kazuhisa,

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:25.790
you forgot the debt you owed 
the Sou Clan, joined the Mongols,

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:28.360
and attempted to destroy our island.

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:29.420
Your crime is unforgivable.

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:33.680
This head will be hung at the castle gate,

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:35.920
or thrown off the side of the road.

00:05:36.570 --> 00:05:38.590
We shall deal with it as clan law decrees.

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:41.130
You have no complaint, Jinzaburou?

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:44.240
Do as you like.

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:56.290
<i>Shiraishi...</i>

00:05:57.150 --> 00:05:59.300
<i>You now dwell in the underworld.</i>

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:04.330
<i>You'll watch over us there, won't you?</i>

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:14.860
<i>And so, the sun fell 
on the night of October 9th.</i>

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:22.280
The fire will disappear 
by the day after tomorrow.

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:27.080
It will take many years 
for the forest to regrow.

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:28.930
Once the war is over,

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:31.280
we shall build a shrine 
to our ancestors once more

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:32.860
and remember the dead.

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:36.320
We must build a grave 
for the Mongols, as well.

00:06:37.510 --> 00:06:39.090
It's ready.

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:41.800
This is the boar meat 
that Shiraishi left us.

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:43.650
You don't want any?

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:45.040
Hell no.

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:46.710
He was a traitor.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:48.980
More for me, then.

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:53.670
It's no fun being alone.

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:55.330
What's wrong, old man?

00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:57.260
You're not eating?

00:06:58.320 --> 00:06:59.460
Hey...

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:02.150
There's something I want you to see.

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:20.070
<i>Amazing.</i>

00:07:20.070 --> 00:07:22.130
<i>Is that how a samurai is supposed to behave?</i>

00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:25.070
<i>The war isn't over.</i>

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:33.420
I'll avenge my father...

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:35.890
You.

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:37.850
You're Ginshichi's son, aren't you?

00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:40.400
Sasamaru, you need to become strong, too,

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:42.600
and avenge your father!

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:43.770
No.

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:47.480
You need to get stronger
 and challenge him to a duel.

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:49.850
It's cowardly to attack him in his sleep.

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:58.360
<i>You're a man who tempts others to sin.</i>

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:04.500
<i>Once the battle with the Mongols 
is over, what will you do?</i>

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:07.420
<i>Leave in search of more war?</i>

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:13.040
<i>There's no place left for you now.</i>

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:16.970
<i>Except for this one.</i>

00:08:30.890 --> 00:08:33.130
If you tell anyone...

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:35.650
I don't care if you're a kid. You're dead.

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:44.560
What are you doing?

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:48.960
I came to wake you up.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:51.260
You lazy man.

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:54.430
You tell others that 
the war isn't over, but...

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:57.900
D-Don't blame me if you 
get killed in your sleep.

00:08:57.900 --> 00:09:01.170
It's a war. That's why you 
need to sleep when you can.

00:09:01.670 --> 00:09:03.380
You don't know what will happen.

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:04.940
What happened at the south gate?

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:06.070
I don't know,

00:09:06.070 --> 00:09:08.020
but the magistrate is heading there now.

00:09:08.490 --> 00:09:09.510
See?

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:21.150
We pray for the Mongols' defeat.

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:24.240
Show us the path, we pray.

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:29.130
We will now make our request to the gods.

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:32.520
What is this?

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:35.120
Deer? Boars?

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:36.800
What's going on?

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:40.260
It's like the hunt of some great lord.

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:43.050
Prey chased by many hunters.

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:46.570
What do you mean, Jinzaburou?

00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:50.940
They came here to flee 
from some great army...

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:55.190
But this didn't happen when 
the Mongols came today...

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:59.980
The animals are telling us that 
the next force is a hell of a lot bigger.

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:05.870
There're so many of them that 
there's no place for the animals to hide,

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:09.160
and they're crashing down on us like a wave.

00:10:10.280 --> 00:10:11.460
A huge army?

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:13.960
Even more than this afternoon?

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:16.620
Don't worry, Toibarai.

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:19.070
No matter how many times the Mongols come,

00:10:19.070 --> 00:10:21.910
we can just teach them a lesson 
like we did last time.

00:10:21.910 --> 00:10:24.200
I'm not worried!

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:25.880
I'm ready to fight!

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:30.590
Yeah! We're the only ones 
who can protect Kanatanoki Castle!

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:33.590
You guys are thinking too small.

00:10:33.590 --> 00:10:37.380
Why not, "We're the only ones 
who can protect Tsushima"?

00:10:41.650 --> 00:10:43.170
Morale is high.

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:47.190
If the enemy comes back, 
we can just drive them away.

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:49.660
Eventually, reinforcements will come.

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:54.910
We beg for your guidance.

00:10:54.910 --> 00:11:01.830
Tell us the path that we must follow.

00:11:12.850 --> 00:11:13.840
Elder!

00:11:16.410 --> 00:11:18.070
He's not breathing.

00:11:21.230 --> 00:11:22.810
This is it.

00:11:22.810 --> 00:11:25.680
I found it floating near the coast.

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:29.370
I grabbed it and then hid it here!

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:32.690
When I saw what happened 
to Shiraishi, I realized...

00:11:32.690 --> 00:11:36.200
This place is hell. It's beyond salvation.

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:38.730
There's nothing we can do if we stay here.

00:11:39.370 --> 00:11:42.840
So why don't we all leave?

00:11:44.830 --> 00:11:48.600
I stole food and water 
during the day and loaded it.

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:51.260
We can leave right now!

00:11:54.580 --> 00:11:56.870
There's money I buried in Hakata.

00:11:56.870 --> 00:12:00.330
If you help, you can have a third of it.

00:12:00.330 --> 00:12:01.790
How about it?

00:12:01.790 --> 00:12:04.390
You can't expect us to believe that.

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:08.120
It's even got sails?

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:09.630
It sure does.

00:12:09.630 --> 00:12:12.240
See? Sturdy ones.

00:12:14.180 --> 00:12:15.740
This wind...

00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:21.500
If we ride the anaji winds,
we can get to Kyushu.

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:23.500
We'll have to take 
the long way around, then.

00:12:24.830 --> 00:12:26.670
I didn't expect you to be into it.

00:12:26.670 --> 00:12:29.250
Amushi, what about you?

00:12:29.250 --> 00:12:31.390
You want to go back to the capital, right?

00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:35.450
Well, sure...

00:12:41.020 --> 00:12:43.670
Hell, no, you stupid old man!

00:12:44.870 --> 00:12:47.630
What about you, Hitari? Douen?

00:12:47.630 --> 00:12:50.200
I'll look for a bigger ship.

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:52.170
I don't want to go through 
what I did to get here.

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:53.750
I'll pass, too.

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:56.820
You young kids are wimps.

00:12:56.820 --> 00:12:58.720
Okay, off I go.

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:03.370
I see.

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:04.380
You're going?

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:06.160
Well, stay safe.

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:08.380
You, too.

00:13:08.380 --> 00:13:12.510
Just don't end up dying next to Kuchii.

00:13:12.510 --> 00:13:13.580
Yeah.

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:15.150
We'll be careful.

00:13:20.290 --> 00:13:22.240
So you're fleeing the island, coward.

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:24.750
You were here, too?

00:13:24.750 --> 00:13:28.180
You wanted to run, didn't you, Amushi?

00:13:28.180 --> 00:13:31.010
Run? Hell no.

00:13:31.010 --> 00:13:34.250
Well, I'm willing to leave the island 
whenever I can, though.

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:37.040
Then, do it now!

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:38.490
Hurry!

00:13:38.490 --> 00:13:40.200
Stop it, fool!

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:42.270
The boat's gone!

00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:44.560
What were you even thinking—

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:51.360
This has never happened before.

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:52.760
How awful...

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:54.830
A terrible omen!

00:13:56.270 --> 00:13:59.140
No, it's not.

00:13:59.140 --> 00:14:03.530
It's a sign that the disaster 
that has befallen us has passed.

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:09.540
The elder has sacrificed himself for us.

00:14:10.460 --> 00:14:11.500
But...

00:14:11.500 --> 00:14:13.460
The priestesses shall continue to pray.

00:14:18.740 --> 00:14:21.540
Magistrate, what did the omens say?

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:26.350
The omens say that this disaster 
will turn into good fortune for us.

00:14:26.350 --> 00:14:28.260
And thus, we will win!

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:31.590
We will? Great!

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:35.090
Morale will only get higher.

00:14:38.670 --> 00:14:40.450
Turn into good fortune?

00:14:40.450 --> 00:14:41.740
Good to hear.

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:45.980
It's true that if we decide to eat 
those animals, we'll survive the winter.

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:49.550
But it's only boars and deer.

00:14:49.550 --> 00:14:52.020
Are there no foxes, tanuki, 
or rabbits on this island?

00:14:52.020 --> 00:14:55.020
We've only heard of them in stories.

00:14:56.430 --> 00:14:58.680
This place isn't secret anymore.

00:14:58.680 --> 00:15:00.670
They can come whenever they like.

00:15:01.590 --> 00:15:05.340
The scouts are dispersed 
deep within the forest.

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:08.660
If something happens, 
they'll give the signal.

00:15:12.240 --> 00:15:13.860
Hey, look.

00:15:18.650 --> 00:15:20.260
There's about twenty of them?

00:15:20.260 --> 00:15:22.270
Yeah. Signal the castle.

00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:25.490
Hurry! Signal the castle!

00:15:25.490 --> 00:15:26.650
I'm sorry!

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:31.810
General Kou Chakyuu!

00:15:31.810 --> 00:15:33.790
The vice marshal is here, personally?

00:15:33.790 --> 00:15:37.500
Fool. Don't let your guard down 
around the bugs. Crush them all.

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:40.720
No matter how much we outnumber them!

00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:45.290
What kills more allies than 
anything isn't the enemy's blade,

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:47.120
it's their scouts!

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:47.550
<b>Mongol Army Vice Marshal (Eastern Expeditionary Force) 
Kou Chakyuu</b>

00:15:47.540 --> 00:15:49.310
I'm sorry, sir!

00:15:49.310 --> 00:15:52.030
We messed up and they found us...

00:15:52.030 --> 00:15:54.300
I'll have the torches put out immediately.

00:15:56.050 --> 00:15:57.120
No.

00:15:57.120 --> 00:15:59.320
We've got the darkness on our side.

00:15:59.320 --> 00:16:01.810
Let's show them, instead.

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:03.690
Let them see what we look like!

00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:09.100
Magistrate, fire half a league away.

00:16:09.100 --> 00:16:10.620
Is it one of ours?

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:13.070
Did they find the Mongols?

00:16:18.100 --> 00:16:18.820
There're more?

00:16:25.530 --> 00:16:27.340
There're so many...

00:16:27.740 --> 00:16:29.610
Those aren't our scouts.

00:16:30.130 --> 00:16:32.250
That's the Mongol army.

00:16:32.250 --> 00:16:33.740
Wake everyone up.

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:35.020
Yes, sir.

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:39.130
Wow! Those are all enemies?

00:16:39.130 --> 00:16:42.840
Onitakemaru sure chose 
the right time to run.

00:16:44.220 --> 00:16:45.350
Onitakemaru?

00:16:46.590 --> 00:16:47.480
Yeah.

00:16:48.340 --> 00:16:49.610
I see.

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:51.360
He ran?

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:53.800
I should've gotten on the boat, too.

00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:55.660
I screwed up this time.

00:16:56.910 --> 00:16:58.150
Listen to you.

00:16:58.580 --> 00:17:01.460
Have we ever not screwed up?

00:17:02.220 --> 00:17:05.980
I didn't think you'd flee with me.

00:17:05.980 --> 00:17:09.120
I thought you were another 
do-gooder like Jinzaburou.

00:17:10.240 --> 00:17:12.130
Don't compare me to him!

00:17:12.740 --> 00:17:13.770
No...

00:17:14.210 --> 00:17:15.920
Hell no.

00:17:15.920 --> 00:17:20.270
If you think he's a good guy 
like I am, you're wrong.

00:17:20.840 --> 00:17:25.520
He's only interested in war itself.

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:27.820
The man you see now is a fake.

00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:33.170
I'd been wishing for a chance to fight 
him again and bring him low, but...

00:17:34.040 --> 00:17:36.060
Forget it.

00:17:36.590 --> 00:17:40.730
His eyes don't make me shiver 
like they did before.

00:17:43.490 --> 00:17:46.840
That army will be here by dawn.

00:17:47.280 --> 00:17:50.240
When that happens, this place will 
be like the bottom of a boiling pot.

00:17:50.240 --> 00:17:51.620
Nowhere to run.

00:17:53.400 --> 00:17:57.210
Shouldn't we jump out of the pot, then?

00:17:57.210 --> 00:17:59.280
Magistrate Nagamine,

00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:02.510
let's abandon the castle before they arrive.

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:05.740
Our priority is to survive!

00:18:06.860 --> 00:18:10.730
Princess Teruhi, that's what they want.

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:17.360
They're showing us their army to get 
us to flee the castle before the fight.

00:18:17.360 --> 00:18:21.010
You just don't want 
to give up the castle, right?

00:18:21.010 --> 00:18:24.220
The Toibarai have kept 
this castle for generations...

00:18:26.110 --> 00:18:29.380
Then let your people run.

00:18:30.060 --> 00:18:32.230
The snow will fall in a month.

00:18:32.230 --> 00:18:34.290
With no food and no shelter,

00:18:34.290 --> 00:18:35.870
everyone will freeze to death.

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:39.100
The Toibarai will remain here.

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:42.780
Die now or die in a month?

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:46.520
If that's the question, I'm out.

00:18:46.870 --> 00:18:49.250
But there's one other way.

00:18:49.250 --> 00:18:52.700
Abandon the castle temporarily 
and wait for reinforcements.

00:18:52.700 --> 00:18:56.690
We can survive until 
they get in their mountains.

00:18:57.510 --> 00:19:01.190
You believe that reinforcements 
are coming from Hakata?

00:19:02.020 --> 00:19:06.450
Whatever you decide, to fight 
or to stay here, decide now.

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:08.460
It's practically too late already.

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:13.810
When we met with Emperor Antoku, he said...

00:19:13.810 --> 00:19:17.670
If you want to win, you need to survive!

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:21.420
As long as someone survives, we win!

00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:26.180
You want me to sit by as 
the Mongols pillage our mountain?

00:19:27.160 --> 00:19:30.840
So that at least a few of us can survive?

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:34.050
Very well.

00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:37.350
Get everyone out of the castle 
and into the wilderness!

00:19:37.350 --> 00:19:38.440
Magistrate!

00:19:39.060 --> 00:19:42.990
The men in the watchtowers say 
they see what looks like a fleet at sea.

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:43.900
What?

00:19:44.800 --> 00:19:46.870
Reinforcements are here?

00:19:47.520 --> 00:19:49.610
What is that?

00:19:49.610 --> 00:19:52.380
Ships? From Hakata?

00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:27.640
 Hakata, Kyushu

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:31.850
We're about 70 percent done loading the ships.

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:33.160
All that's left is boarding the men.

00:21:33.160 --> 00:21:34.970
Get them aboard first.

00:21:34.970 --> 00:21:36.440
Dawn comes soon.

00:21:36.440 --> 00:21:38.470
Once the men are here, leave immediately.

00:21:38.470 --> 00:21:39.640
Yes, sir!

00:21:41.220 --> 00:21:43.830
Kagesuke, what is this?

00:21:43.830 --> 00:21:45.190
Father?

00:21:45.190 --> 00:21:48.270
I didn't hear anything about 
an expedition to Tsushima.

00:21:45.490 --> 00:21:48.280
<b>Shouni Clan Patriarch  
Shouni Sukeyoshi</b>

00:21:48.270 --> 00:21:50.010
Please allow me to do this.

00:21:50.010 --> 00:21:52.450
I'm sending my own men.

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:55.310
You've got a damn good reason, I'm sure.

00:21:55.310 --> 00:21:57.710
We'll delay the Mongols at Tsushima.

00:21:57.710 --> 00:22:01.340
If we can hold them a month, 
until the snow starts to fall...

00:22:01.340 --> 00:22:03.920
They'll retreat.

00:22:03.920 --> 00:22:05.510
A fantasy.

00:22:06.250 --> 00:22:09.800
My son, you're not looking 
at what comes next.

00:22:09.800 --> 00:22:13.080
Are the Mongols our only enemy?

00:22:13.080 --> 00:22:16.110
What if we lose men before the great war,

00:22:16.110 --> 00:22:18.600
and the other clans win more glory than us?

00:22:19.110 --> 00:22:21.300
After the war, when the Mongols are gone,

00:22:21.300 --> 00:22:23.830
it will change who runs Kyushu.

00:22:24.500 --> 00:22:27.270
We've done a great job with Tsushima.

00:22:27.270 --> 00:22:31.880
Our clan's representative, 
Sou Sukekuni, has done his duty.

00:22:31.880 --> 00:22:36.010
We shall ensure their prosperity 
for a millennia to come.

00:22:36.010 --> 00:22:38.700
But how is that possible, when...

00:22:38.700 --> 00:22:41.330
The war in Tsushima is over.

00:22:41.330 --> 00:22:42.870
Now, it's our turn.

00:22:42.870 --> 00:22:44.840
There will be no reinforcements.

00:22:44.840 --> 00:22:46.870
Unload the ships!

00:22:48.040 --> 00:22:50.560
Wait, Father!

00:22:50.560 --> 00:22:54.000
The people of Tsushima are 
under our protection!

00:22:54.000 --> 00:22:56.050
My lord, the patriarch has spoken.

00:22:58.880 --> 00:23:04.610
Are you saying you don't care 
what happens to Tsushima now, Father?

00:23:06.270 --> 00:23:07.310
That's it.

00:23:07.310 --> 00:23:11.410
The scouts on the beach 
say those ships are...

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:13.580
Mongol warships!

00:23:15.550 --> 00:23:17.660
They're not reinforcements?

00:23:17.660 --> 00:23:21.770
Reinforcements from Hakata 
would land on the south side of the island.

00:23:21.770 --> 00:23:24.240
But that's the north side.

00:23:24.240 --> 00:23:25.660
We're surrounded, huh?

00:23:26.350 --> 00:23:30.050
Ships from the castle's north 
and a huge army from the south.

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:32.170
We're trapped like rats.

00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:36.670
Tomorrow's one hell of a lucky day.

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:40.010
<b>Episode 10: 
Bad Omen</b>
